# Groundwork — mechanical enforcement of the canon-change rule.
#
# The design package is canon. Every change to it is approved by the named design owner. This
# is not a courtesy review: it is the only thing standing between "the design describes the
# system" and "the design describes what someone once intended".
#
# Replace @design-owner with the actual handle or team.

design/            @design-owner
SPRINT.md          @design-owner

# The gate register is the go-live decision record. A gate closed without a dated observation
# is rejected in review, and this line is what guarantees someone reads it.
design/go-live-readiness.md   @design-owner

# ADRs are immutable once accepted. A diff that edits an existing ADR's body — rather than
# adding a new one and flipping a status line — is the thing this entry exists to catch.
design/adr/        @design-owner

# The workflow's own configuration.
.groundwork.yaml   @design-owner
